[{"id":"VRCE-4-48-1","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":48,"verse":1,"english":"Then the eminently wise Angada, fatigued, spoke to all the monkeys, cheering them.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-49-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4048001","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"70e62418a656edade99e37ac122dc514034a1fcd0da0b908e6c393e5eb4c8409","compact":"3a46c7bd56d5442b8ecb26398f8b1626a68b8f9ea1d73dd197bbcd5610f38669","nasal":"ca66f6a2986638fdaf71f8ac8f0093c5560e4bd3be5b447be869602b071f59fb"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-48-2","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":48,"verse":2,"english":"Woods, and mountains, and rivers, and impenetrable wilds, and valleys, and mountain caverns have been thoroughly searched. But Jānakī we have failed to find anywhere,—or that wicked wight, the Rākṣasa that has ravished Sītā.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.661,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-49-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4048002","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2849c51c51b6100513380cef5559c6164b94c357a7696282d184a888cc6f9f5e","compact":"d81bf1a0b6dab25a7166ff426773e1435da8c0a72ba5f926e232e320eb78be16","nasal":"96b6e89265b537f57fff715f474d1a1d17d131867966e1998c0dc85fda896d0f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-48-3","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":48,"verse":3,"english":"Woods, and mountains, and rivers, and impenetrable wilds, and valleys, and mountain caverns have been thoroughly searched. But Jānakī we have failed to find anywhere,—or that wicked wight, the Rākṣasa that has ravished Sītā.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.474,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-49-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4048003","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b876fa74b0d4fdfe4b83c99cb10cf8b25bbc54459a62a78f8f5b52ab62359d77","compact":"b9be8ce677c26e0439b8c53b55b49c223a31cdc033dcd56d44b8a54edd78813c","nasal":"b9be8ce677c26e0439b8c53b55b49c223a31cdc033dcd56d44b8a54edd78813c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-48-4","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":48,"verse":4,"english":"We have spent a great part of the term that had been assigned by Sugrīva of stern commands. Therefore, banishing languor, sadness, and invading drowsiness, do you together search all round.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-49-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4048004","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b842c9ee57c15177ca51d3c9098e3c853b6c46d0391888a7552fad88040e5788","compact":"be8e7f42f830c175480c4f3a39e0754d058f718f4fc287e12f840870fabeed95","nasal":"df6479bed2f528f534227834b7318026668b81ac4c35dca39bc484d039e3f7f8"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-48-5","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":48,"verse":5,"english":"Do you so search Sītā, that she may be found out (by us). High spirits, ability and forwardness in action, are said to conduce to success. Therefore it is that I speak thus to you.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-49-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4048005","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d08b363973f7e1ef3815cd7b69eb12443a581b0f4178ce7e553eb0eab6c6176c","compact":"390639e230f3b4f2ee160fed0bd4a1d445fdb86baf1fd9ede1e3ab4a9fdd8b80","nasal":"192ed03647d2e1554816ac4681699c0aec89c98f6dca6d8c25463d0fb8dd99b3"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-48-6","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":48,"verse":6,"english":"Do you so search Sītā, that she may be found out (by us). High spirits, ability and forwardness in action, are said to conduce to success. Therefore it is that I speak thus to you.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-49-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4048006","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"921640a82cf1bc329ebaf311edcb76a894238bf77e1077f39584af1cc3c5121c","compact":"3321b99e28077f9be9a9c1e3c1e10aa7f3574ecf2ea5019b4b856383f8a5af3e","nasal":"3321b99e28077f9be9a9c1e3c1e10aa7f3574ecf2ea5019b4b856383f8a5af3e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-48-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":48,"verse":7,"english":"You dwellers of the wood, do you to day rummage this impenetrable wood; renouncing grief, do you again search through this forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.818,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-49-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4048007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"69e44d9fa7c070fbd26822726e11ca09b6d6d1fb73c5249404604d60719a530b","compact":"4b32319712267dd63dcb17bb3755708b31fd2b0803bb97911cd638d983840535","nasal":"c768c600879d0769c203a83f9ec2c28c4cae12692c897b06722fcca5a84731a3"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-48-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":48,"verse":8,"english":"Those who act, for certain behold the fruit of their endeavours; but if people once give way to grief, they cannot again attain vigour.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.441,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-49-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4048008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3bd8504a761f398965f59f290c45d5d7d55196a423beec580e19ea8a7a008889","compact":"9cdc94098b92a29705ec1ec35843006607e4fe326a64458106ed03862e35be20","nasal":"9cdc94098b92a29705ec1ec35843006607e4fe326a64458106ed03862e35be20"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-48-9","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":48,"verse":9,"english":"You monkeys, king Sugrīva is irascible; and inflicteth sharp punishments. He should be always feared, as also the magnanimous Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-49-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4048009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"388836758daf483a45b6dda5e8cc206cf7290fdd353c12c2a8e089b4f5c0ad9f","compact":"8d74e32d271391909d2e21271914706b21bdc17903e8eadf6c20d17799757138","nasal":"50608835481903273397fd4c4b3fcd4efa20827e03de5d1d59757dc094695229"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-48-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":48,"verse":10,"english":"I tell you this for your good. Act accordingly, if you list. And do you also express what else you are capable of.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.694,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-49-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4048010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6252f3f531714085089dfbda2758486f824e43d1fa23625bddb5d8ad01db68d2","compact":"eac02b56ea0c28fbae2d13cab97dd6be41818265c15414d8a77f72f6f82a080d","nasal":"b918eb4851cc7193ae10228eff03fbb894abc8b4084b78c88371faead3246425"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-48-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":48,"verse":11,"english":"Hearing Angada's words Gandhamādana said in candid words faint from thirst and fatigue,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-49-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4048011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"492b50f7aa71e9a6d81ce2a3c845b95711dc16f32a69dafebd8d385b8f653e0e","compact":"785479f60adbc215f733fa130536cdf0f4bca2c1842e82edfe8babd1cbdea42f","nasal":"1281e031266d463c0f489f9a76522fd14253deaec9c67eb215bd9086496dd6b9"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-48-12","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":48,"verse":12,"english":"What Angada has said to us is worthy of him, and is beneficial and good. Do you follow his speech.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-49-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4048012","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e0315eaf0e1785d73b19ce402ba5d2225a94fd17df6e74f3bec570448eacf6ff","compact":"91b7dec6f7c1f495bc19160921a8b59522bb734d1c445a0eb098e97b6bfa9fac","nasal":"735158f40f937fb3651d89c9fec1c93aafc0d6de7320cd98b255ad25ef903ec1"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-48-13","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":48,"verse":13,"english":"Let us afresh search hills, caves and rocks, vacant forests and mountain cascades,-in accordance with what the high-souled Sugrīva has laid down. Let all in a body rummage the wood, and the mountain caverns.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.841,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-49-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4048013","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b4beea26c65c8a7fe90f82e71981add8e591932717feaabe8d7e9e573abeab94","compact":"aa71fd24c9825fa5262179aa76882a46c168aefdd9b9921266ad7f4ba59fa0ff","nasal":"dec64a2f8598e2e553f0b5dcc9822fdb33cabac277ff35c9a60a86067bca2208"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-48-14","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":48,"verse":14,"english":"Let us afresh search hills, caves and rocks, vacant forests and mountain cascades,-in accordance with what the high-souled Sugrīva has laid down. Let all in a body rummage the wood, and the mountain caverns.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.806,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-49-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4048014","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_finger